<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 27 May, from 1564 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/john-calvin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-calvin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1564 CE <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Calvin dies in Geneva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The French reformer died aged 54 in the city he had shaped into a Protestant model. His Institutes of the Christian Religion influenced Reformed churches from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1703 CE <span class="tih-ago">323 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter the Great founds St Petersburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Construction began on the Peter and Paul Fortress on an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva</a>, on land newly taken from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Peter made the city his capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s 'window on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1937 CE <span class="tih-ago">89 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Golden Gate Bridge opens to pedestrians</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 200,000 people walked across the new bridge on its opening day before cars were allowed the next. Its main span was then the longest of any suspension bridge.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1941 CE <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royal Navy sinks the battleship Bismarck</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crippled by a torpedo hit to her rudder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bismarck-battleship">Bismarck</a> was pounded by British battleships and sank in the Atlantic. Only about 114 of her crew of over 2,000 survived.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1967 CE <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Australians vote to include Aboriginal people in the census</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Over 90 per cent voted to count Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people in the population and to let the Commonwealth make laws for them. It remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s most successful referendum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li></ol>
